==English==
{{was wotd|2015|December|26}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|nl|gulpen|t=to gush, pour forth, guzzle, swallow eagerly}}, from {{der|en|dum|gulpen}}, {{m|dum|golpen}}, related to {{cog|fy|gjalpe}}, {{m|fy|gjalpje}}, {{m|fy|gjealpje|t=to gush, spurt forth}}, {{cog|da|gulpe}}, {{m|da|gylpe|t=to gulp up, disgorge}}, dialectal {{cog|sv|glapa|t=to gulp down}}, {{cog|ang|gealpettan|t=to gulp down, eat greedily, devour}}. More at {{l|en|galp}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɡʌlp/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The usual amount [[swallow]]ed.
#* '''1898''', {{w|J. Meade Falkner}}, {{w|Moonfleet}} Chapter 4
#*: What the liquor was I do not know, but it was not so strong but that I could swallow it in great '''gulps''' and found it less burning than my burning throat.
# The sound of swallowing.
# A sound of swallowing indicating fear.
#* {{RQ:Sinclair Jungle|17}}
#*: Little Stanislovas was also trembling, and all but too frightened to speak. "They — they sent me to tell you — " he said, with a '''gulp'''.
#* '''1994''', James Charles Collins, Jerry I. Porras, ''Built to Last: Successful Habits of Visionary Companies''
#*: Indeed, the envisioned future should produce a bit of "the '''gulp''' factor" […], there should be an almost audible "'''gulp'''".

